<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 45,100 in December.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 45,100 in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in December and average earnings in November (Previous estimates in brackets, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>    UNEMPLOYMENT		     DEC	 NOV    (NOV PREL)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		  -45,100   -95,400  (-95,800)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			 6.7	 6.9     (6.9)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change    -3,200     n/a     (-105,800)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate (pct) 6.7	 6.7     (6.7)</p>
<p>NOTE - Market consensus was for 30,000 fall in unemployment  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million)     1,884.7   1,929.8   (1.929)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj     1,868.2   1,871.4   (1.871)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m adj   -62,000   -59,600  (-59,800)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	 -44,300   -39,400  (-39,500)</p>
<p>    AVERAGE EARNINGS		  NOV	 OCT    (OCT PREL)</p>
<p>    underlying yearly chng (pct)  4.0	 4.0	  (4.0)</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)		134.2     133.6     (133.7)</p>
<p>    actual yearly chng (pct)	4.0	 3.7	  (3.8)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>    Production-- underlying	 4.25	4.25     (4.25)</p>
<p>		  -- actual	     4.5	 3.9	  (3.8)</p>
<p>    Manufacturing-- underlying    4.5	 4.5	 (4.25)</p>
<p>		     -- actual	  4.7	 4.2	  (4.0)</p>
<p>    Services     -- underlying    3.75	4.0	  (4.0)</p>
<p>		     -- actual	  3.6	 3.7	  (3.8)</p>
<p>NOTE-consensus forecast 4.0 pct for underlying average earnings</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS	    NOV	  OCT     (PREL OCT)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago 4.1	  3.6	 (3.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  115.3	114.4   (114.0)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago 4.2	  4.6	 (4.6)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  114.8	114.5   (114.2)</p>
<p>    Job centre vacancies     DEC	  NOV     (PREL NOV)</p>
<p>    Change			-1,200     +6,100   (+7,100)</p>
<p>    Avge 3-m change	   +4,600     +110,600  (+10.900)</p>
<p>The ONS said the workforce in employment in the UK was 26,076,000 in September 1996. This represents a rise of 200,000 in the third quarter and a rise of 299,000 over the year to September. The ONS said it is difficult to quantify the extent to which the latest jobless figures are affected by the introduction of the jobseekers allowance, but said it would have accounted for a maximum of 10,000 of December's jobless fall. )8/&amp; )8/&amp;</p>
</text>
